To use the `updateAAD` method in the AEAD GCM cipher class for authentication, you need to follow these steps:

1. Import the necessary classes:
```java
import javax.crypto.AEADBadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.AEADCipher;
import javax.crypto.spec.IvParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;
```
2. Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class:
```java
AEADCipher aeadCipher = AEADCipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
```
3. Set the secret key and initialization vector (IV):
```java
SecretKeySpec secretKeySpec = new SecretKeySpec("your_secret_key".getBytes(), "AES");
IvParameterSpec ivParameterSpec = new IvParameterSpec("your_iv".getBytes());
aeadCipher.init(AEADCipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, secretKeySpec, ivParameterSpec);
```
4. Update the authentication tag (AAD) using the `updateAAD` method:
```java
byte[] aad = "your_authentication_tag".getBytes();
aeadCipher.updateAAD(aad);
```
5. Encrypt or decrypt data using the `doFinal` method:
```java
byte[] encryptedData = aeadCipher.doFinal(your_data.getBytes()); // For encryption
byte[] decryptedData = aeadCipher.doFinal(encryptedData); // For decryption
```

Remember to replace `"your_secret_key"` and `"your_iv"` with your actual secret key and IV values. Also, make sure to handle exceptions appropriately when using the cipher class.

