To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new model class in your NestJS project using the `@Model()` decorator from the `@nestjs/mongodb` package.
2. Define the schema for each field of your document using the `@Prop()` decorator. You can use the `@Schema()` decorator to define custom schemas for your fields.
3. Use the `@Document()` decorator to specify the collection name for your documents.
4. Implement the `save()` method to create a new document in your collection.

Here's an example of how you can implement this:
```typescript
import { Model, Prop, Schema, Document } from '@nestjs/mongodb';

@Model({ collection: 'my-collection' })
export class MyModel {
  @Prop()
  @Schema({ type: String })
  name: string;

  @Prop()
  @Schema({ type: Number })
  age: number;

  @Prop()
  @Schema({ type: Boolean })
  isActive: boolean;

  async save(): Promise<MyModel> {
    const document = await this.model.create(this);
    return document;
  }
}
```
In this example, we have defined a `MyModel` class that has three properties: `name`, `age`, and `isActive`. We have also defined custom schemas for each property using the `@Schema()` decorator. Finally, we have implemented the `save()` method to create a new document in our collection.

