To import your relational data from Microsoft SQL Database to Neo4j, you can use the APOC (Awesome Procedures On Call) library's `neo4j-import` procedure. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. Install the APOC library in your Neo4j database by running the following command in the Neo4j Browser:

```cypher
CALL gds.install('apoc');
```

2. Create a Cypher script to import your data. Replace the placeholders with your actual table names and column names:

```cypher
// Import Account nodes
WITH [
  {id: x.accountID, label: 'Account', properties: {accountID: x.accountID, AccountGUID: x.AccountGUID}}
  | x IN (SELECT * FROM Account)
] AS accounts
MERGE (a:Account {id: a.id})
SET a = a.properties;

// Import Group nodes
WITH [
  {id: x.GroupID, label: 'Group', properties: {GroupID: x.GroupID, GroupGUID: x.GroupGUID}}
  | x IN (SELECT * FROM Group)
] AS groups
MERGE (g:Group {id: g.id})
SET g = g.properties;

// Import GroupAccount relationships
WITH [
  {srcId: x.GroupID, trgId: x.AccountID}
  | x IN (SELECT * FROM GroupAccount)
] AS groupAccountRelationships
MERGE (ga:GroupAccount {srcId: ga.srcId, trgId: ga.trgId})
SET ga.properties = {};

// Import GroupMemberGroup relationships
WITH [
  {srcId: x.GroupID, trgId: x.MemberGroupID}
  | x IN (SELECT * FROM GroupMemberGroup)
] AS groupMemberGroupRelationships
MERGE (gmg:GroupMemberGroup {srcId: gmg.srcId, trgId: gmg.trgId})
SET gmg.properties = {};
