To retrieve the username from the JWT token in ASP.NET Core Web API, you can use the `ClaimsPrincipal` object and the `User` property. Here's an example:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization;
using Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens;
using System.Security.Claims;

[Authorize]
public class MyController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpGet]
    public IActionResult GetUsername()
    {
        var user = (ClaimsPrincipal)User;
        var username = user.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier).Value;
        return Ok(username);
    }
}
```

In this example, we first check if the user is authorized to access the controller. If they are, we get the `ClaimsPrincipal` object from the `User` property. Then, we find the claim with the type `ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier`, which typically contains the username. Finally, we return the username as an OK response.

