To achieve this task, you'll need to use PHP with MySQLi (MySQL Improved Extension) or PDO (PHP Data Objects). Here's an example using MySQLi:

1. First, make sure you have PHP and MySQL installed on your server. Then, create a new PHP file (e.g., `identify_loyal_customers.php`) and add the following code:

```php
<?php
// Database connection
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "your_username";
$password = "your_password";
$dbname = "your_database";

$conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

// Check connection
if ($conn->connect_error) {
    die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
}

// Query to find loyal customers
$sql = "SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) as purchase_count
        FROM transactions
        WHERE product_id = 'specific_product_id'
        GROUP BY customer_id
        HAVING purchase_count >= 3
        AND DATEDIFF(CURDATE(), purchase_date) <= 7"; // Limit results to within last week

$result = $conn->query($sql);

if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
    // output data of each row
    while($row = $result->fetch_assoc()) {
        echo "Customer ID: " . $row["customer_id"]. " - Purchase Count: " . $row["purchase_count"]. "<br>";
    }
} else {
    echo "0 results";
}

$conn->close();
?>
```

Replace `"your_username"`, `"your_password"`, and `"your_database"` with your actual MySQL credentials and database name. Also, replace `"specific_product_id"` with the actual ID of the product you want to track.

2. Save the file and upload it to your web server.

3. Access the file through your web browser by typing the URL of the file into the address bar. For example, if the file is saved in the root directory of your web server, you would

To achieve this, you'll need to use SQL (Structured Query Language) with your PHP program. Here's an example of how you can modify the query to group by customer ID, count the number of purchases for each product, and filter out customers who haven't made at least three purchases of the specified product within a week:

```php
<?php
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "username";
$password = "password";
$dbname = "database_name";

// Create connection
$conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

// Check connection
if ($conn->connect_error) {
    die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
}

// Set up the SQL query
$sql = "SELECT 
    c.customer_id, 
    c.first_name, 
    c.last_name, 
    COUNT(p.product_id) AS purchase_count, 
    p.product_name
FROM 
    customers c
JOIN 
    transactions t ON c.customer_id = t.customer_id
JOIN 
    products p ON t.product_id = p.product_id
WHERE 
    p.product_name = 'specific_product_name'
GROUP BY 
    c.customer_id
HAVING 
    purchase_count >= 3 AND DATEDIFF(CURDATE(), t.transaction_date) <= 7;";

// Execute the query
$result = $conn->query($sql);

// Loop through the results
if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
    // output data of each row
    while($row = $result->fetch_assoc()) {
        echo "Customer Name: " . $row["first_name"] . " " . $row["last_name"] . "<br>";
