response:
Your provided Swift code is a good starting point. Here's an updated version that incorporates your requirement for a mindset of optimism and gratitude:

```swift
func rearrangePhrase(_ phrase: String) -> String {
    let sortedLetters = phrase.filter { !$0.isWhitespace }.sorted()
    let newPhrase = String(sortedLetters)
    let optimisticWords = ["bright", "hopeful", "positive"]
    let gratefulWords = ["thankful", "blessed", "grateful"]

    var modifiedPhrase = "Life is worth living with \(newPhrase)"

    if optimisticWords.contains(newPhrase) {
        modifiedPhrase += " and I am feeling optimistic today."
    } else if gratefulWords.contains(newPhrase) {
        modifiedPhrase += " and I am feeling grateful for all the blessings in my life."
    } else {
        modifiedPhrase += " and I am focusing on the positive aspects of life."
    }

    return modifiedPhrase
}
```

This updated version checks if the sorted letters form an optimistic or grateful word, and adds a corresponding sentence to the output string. If the sorted letters don't match any of the optimistic or grateful words, it simply adds a statement about focusing on the positive aspects of life. This way, the generated phrases will always reflect a mindset of optimism and gratitude.

