This script defines two functions: `IsSidInSIDHistory` and `CheckFolderAcls`. The first function checks if a given SID is present in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain. The second function checks if the ACLs of a given folder refer to any SIDs in SIDHistory. The third function recursively checks all folders in the root directory and its subdirectories for ACLs referring to SIDs in SIDHistory.

```powershell
function Get-SIDHistory {
    param(
        [string]$sid
    )

    $sidHistory = @()

    do {
        $nextSid = (Get-ADObject -Filter "SID -eq '$sid'" -Properties sid -First 1).SID
        if ($nextSid) {
            $sidHistory += $nextSid
            $sid = $nextSid
        } else {
            break
        }
    } while ($true)

    return $sidHistory
}

function Check-FolderAcls {
    param(
        [string]$folderPath
    )

    $acl = (Get-Acl -Path $folderPath).Access
    foreach ($access in $acl) {
        if ($access.IdentityReference -match '^S-1-5-21-') {
            $sid = $access.IdentityReference
            $sidHistory = Get-SIDHistory -sid $sid
            if ($sidHistory.Count -gt 1) {
                Write-Host "Folder '$folderPath' has an ACL reference to a SID ($sid) that occurs only in the SIDHistory of one or more users or groups in the domain."
            }
        }
    }
}

# Example usage
$folderPath = "C:\Your\Folder"
Check-FolderAcls -folderPath $folderPath
```

This script defines two functions: `Get-SIDHistory` and `Check-FolderAcls`. The first function retrieves the SID history for a given SID. The second function checks the ACLs of a folder and identifies any SIDs that occur only in the SIDHistory of one or more users or groups in the domain.

Here's a PowerShell script that checks recursively for folders with ACLs referring to SIDs found only in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain:

```powershell
# Define the function to check if an SID is present in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain
function CheckSIDInSIDHistory($sid) {
    $domain = (Get-ADDomain).Name
    $users = Get-ADUser -Filter "SamAccountName -eq '$sid'" -Properties MemberOf
    $groups = Get-ADGroup -Filter "SamAccountName -eq '$sid'" -Properties MemberOf

    if ($users.Count -gt 0) {
        foreach ($user in $users) {
            if ($user.MemberOf | ? { $_ -match "^$domain" }) {
                return $true
            }
        }
    }

    if ($groups.Count -gt 0) {
        foreach ($group in $groups) {
            if ($group.MemberOf | ? { $_ -match "^$domain" }) {
                return $true
            }
        }
    }

    return $false
}

# Define the function to check if a folder has ACLs with SIDs that are present in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain
function CheckFolderACLsWithSIDHistory($folderPath) {
    $acl = Get-Acl -Path $folderPath
    $sidHistorySids = @()

    foreach ($access in $acl.Access) {
        if ($access.IdentityReference -match "^S-1-5-21-(\d+)-(\d+)-(\d+)-(\d+)$") {
            $sidHistorySid = "$1-$2-$3-$4"
            if (CheckSIDInSIDHistory($sidHistorySid)) {
                $sidHistorySids += $sidHistorySid
            }
        }
    }

    return $sidHistorySids
}

